<title>HUNGARY: Hungary insurers invest HUF212bln by end Q1 - report.</title>
<headline>Hungary insurers invest HUF212bln by end Q1 - report.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungarian insurance firms have invested 212.2 billion forints until the end of March, a 107 percent rise year-on-year, Hungarian news agency MTI Econews said on Tuesday, quoting the State Insurance Supervisory Board.</p>
<p>At the end of March, Hungary's 20 insurance companies held 82 billion in government papers of up to one year maturity, and 72.3 million in government securities of over one year of maturity, it said.</p>
<p>Their investments in shares amounted to 9.87 billion forints, up from 3.45 billion a year ago, while investments in company bonds totalled nine billion forints.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom +36 1 327-4040</p>
